  bootwright / cluster update-admin-credentials
      Generate a fresh password for the existing console administrator of OpenShift or OKD, or
      the dashboard administrator of a managed Ceph cluster. Requires a completed apply and the
      original administrator access. Retains the candidate before updating the cluster; repeat
      an interrupted command to finish the same update. Refuses removed accounts and external
      Ceph. Retrieve the updated credential with cluster info --secrets --name <cluster>. --yes
      skips ordinary confirmation.

  Usage
    bootwright cluster update-admin-credentials [flags]

  Command flags
      --name  Select the exact object name (required)
      --yes   Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright cluster update-admin-credentials --context lab --name cluster
